Market Challenges
Variations in satellite sensitivity, atmospheric conditions and mine operating environments can complicate the detection and attribution of methane emissions. Integrating satellite observations with ground measurements and operational records also requires specialist expertise and additional resources.

Market Restraints
The availability of free public methane alerts and monitoring datasets can limit demand for paid services. In addition, inconsistent reporting enforcement, fragmented monitoring budgets and uncertainty around commercial service pricing may slow wider adoption.

